 of the British and Indian armies. The Chindits saw action in the Burma Campaign and during the Pacific War where they participated in raiding operations against the Imperial Japanese Army. The division often operated deep behind enemy lines and was tasked with attacking enemy forces, facilities and lines of communications. Four members of the Chindits were awarded the Victoria Cross for their services in WWII.","LocalizedString":"The 111th Indian Infantry Brigade was part of the Chindits 3rd Indian Infantry Division of the Indian Army during WWII. The brigade was formed in 1943 in India as part of the Long Range Penetration Brigade which was a special operations unit of the British and Indian armies. The Chindits saw action in the Burma Campaign and during the Pacific War where they participated in raiding operations against the Imperial Japanese Army. The division often operated deep behind enemy lines and was tasked with attacking enemy forces, facilities and lines of communications. Four members of the Chindits were awarded the Victoria Cross for their services in WWII."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Expansion2019","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnBeforeOtherCardGainDefense"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Fury"],"hasFury":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Small'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Small.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Allegiance/t_soldier_empire.t_soldier_empire","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/111th_INDIAN_BRIGADE.111th_INDIAN_BRIGADE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":376.0},"historyPhotoSource":"Imperial War Museum","historyPhotoIdentificationCode":"IND 2290","historyPhotoAuthor":"No 9 Army Film & Photographic Unit","historyPhotoDesc